<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Will Jürgen Klopp's charisma be enough for Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bb3686f63e592c62d0323e1b25defbb9831c7205407fbe7817e0955d1e85fb2</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-j_rgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266--fed309f9f1f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-jürgen-klopp-s-charisma-be-enough-for-germany/a-79455266?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After defeat to Greece, Jürgen Klopp is confronted with the real challenge of his task as Germany head coach. Can his charisma alone push this group forward?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp starts Germany job with shaky Netherlands draw</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6036ae8ad440f3b6d97e2c470a78ad15f732a29105388f440065f5aa8a9bdc0e</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T22:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143--fa995d928e4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A late Netherlands goal denied Jürgen Klopp a win in his first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Germany's football team to 'reclaim the flag'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:057736f0b24fd2dd61dde9254b14a2640f7c867b2712f312a03d4ecaa0741b0f</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610--57ff88db5991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-germany-s-football-team-to-reclaim-the-flag/a-79307610?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp, Germany's new head coach, says he wants his team to reclaim pride in being German after recent political developments.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp and Germany: A partnership long in the making</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e377a1c0b00404e0269d6e81c6eb54314c50456f61abc0bdb352f78df165203e</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-07-24T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-and-germany-a-partnership-long-in-the-making/a-77805100--2614f917074b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-and-germany-a-partnership-long-in-the-making/a-77805100?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In one of the worst-kept secrets in football, the former Dortmund and Liverpool boss has been named head coach of the German men's national team.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>What do Manchester City's charges mean for German football?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:134a7caf8f938ebbcd3c5017f36000956c2aa4f7e2517eb7bb53f3934a37ad15</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412--ba8ebfa60874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manchester City have reportedly been found guilty of major financial rule breaches. What does this mean for German football?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland beat Israel 3-0 in Nations League match overshadowed by political controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:985c887a04f74db83de2f033b9678e5ce9eec185e2c318768d604221606c8ed8</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254--ac737f0c12b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ireland easily beat Israel in a Nations League fixture that 24 hours earlier appeared in doubt. One Irish player pulled out of the match to express his opposition to Israel's actions in the Gaza Strip.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German Olympic Committee names Munich as bid city choice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a05b2e41eda8645caccea2a142c66baeb678b3bba709e2b5604ea1fc2a9b1fd5</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-olympic-committee-names-munich-as-bid-city-choice/a-79441284--424a4614f81d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-olympic-committee-names-munich-as-bid-city-choice/a-79441284?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich has been voted as the city that will bid for the Olympics in 2036, 2040 or 2044. Berlin had been in the running but withdrew on Thursday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bundesliga, other top European leagues call for major FIFA reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46bed9a2bd49450109ad13e5d68cfb88b24537f7345c31fdefe29828d39a2b46</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717--3029f0ff55b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundesliga and three other leading European football leagues have said major reforms to world-governing body FIFA are "essential." However, they stopped short of calling for the resignation of boss Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:322bc36b2dcd21ce6925d8bf6e092d4aa4f636232c059f25fc373bc9837e10f0</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>China's 13-year-old swimming star raises questions on child athletes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97be0297f4fb1226d5b77f63ff0eb074f12a2f7ab90bc17f386c3e3820abc161</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183--95db71a677f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three gold medals and three Asian Games records have catapulted China's Yu Zidi, 13, into the sporting spotlight. She is far from the first teen prodigy, but should teens be competing at elite level?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2202928b8e2b1643db54555bc09c31b9e218f826467d01bd20df918d7a65e88</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU sports commissioner says FIFA is 'damaging to football'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e90b6d59a2e3c675848910ff0c873dfdda580ca17391be813bbe36a0d601bb91</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424--c7a4bd30a298.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking to DW, EU Commissioner Glenn Micallef hit out at world football's governing body over its "poor governance."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Afghanistan's women: A national soccer team without a home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74df50533b287be4dad607760acae0df2802108062a69ba0e7135025ef17eb01</id><updated>2026-09-29T05:53:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500--7cfb666b9c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Afghan women's national football team has finally been officially recognized by FIFA. Now the players want to make history both on and off the field.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
